  "slug": "cross-power-spectrum-b133",
  "summary": "Five November 2026 preprints test theoretical models for tracer cross-correlations against simulations, ahead of DESI and SPHEREx analyses.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is checking theoretical models of tracer auto- and cross-correlations against simulations. Two Lyman-alpha papers test effective field theory: a minimal tree-level EFT for 21 cm and Lyα auto- and cross-spectra at z=2.4-4.2 that constrains the HI and Lyα biases, and a full-shape power spectrum and bispectrum analysis validated on AbacusSummit mocks at z=2.5 for DESI. The SPHEREx pair forecasts cross-correlations of extragalactic background light with CMB lensing; the second paper reports halo-model predictions that match lightcone simulations. The baryonification paper offers two methods for producing thermal SZ Compton-y maps from dark-matter-only lightcones. New here is validation spanning line-intensity, forest, lensing and SZ observables, rather than a single probe.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-22"
}
